speechtext:
Mr. Speaker, we have now had further consultations with respect to certain items. I think you will find that the following motions or draft orders would be agreed to by unanimous consent and passed without debate. These are motions which will help facilitate the transition to the new Standing Orders which take effect on February 24.
If 1 may be permitted, I would read both of these motions. The first is as follows:
That notwithstanding the order adopted by the House on February 13, 1986, in relation to the provincial Standing Orders, effective Monday, February 24, 1986:
1.	All outstanding Orders of Reference before a standing Committee prior to February 24, 1986, shall be deemed referred, with evidence adduced in relation thereto, to the new appropriate corresponding standing committee;
2.	All reports, returns and papers deemed permanently referred to a standing committee pursuant to Standing Orders 47(4) and 70(1), prior to February 24, 1986, shall be deemed permanently referred, with the evidence adduced in relation thereto, to the new appropriate corresponding standing committee;
3.	Where applicable, budgets of any standing committee adopted by the Board of Internal Economy prior to February 24, 1986, shall be deemed to be the budget of the new appropriate corresponding standing committee, unless otherwise ordered by the new committee;
4.	Where applicable, all contracts for the services of staff for a standing committee or sub-committee in effect prior to February 24, 1986, shall be deemed contracts for the services of staff for the new appropriate corresponding standing committee or sub-committee, subject to ratification by the committee chairman;
5.	The Sub-committee on CN Pensions of the Standing Committee on Transport shall continue with its current members and powers, provided that

the sub-committee shall report to the new Standing Committee on Transport no later than April 11, 1986;
6.	The membership of the Striking Committee appointed on Monday, November 5, 1984, shall continue and the said committee shall, within the first ten sitting days following February 23, 1986, prepare and report lists of Members to compose the standing committees and the standing joint committees;
7.	The new provisional Standing Orders relating to the committees of the House, adopted by the House on February 13, 1986, shall come into effect the sitting day following the day on which the report of the Striking Committee is concurred in. Until such day, the provisional and permanent Standing Orders 70, 71 and 72, in effect as of September 9, 1985, shall continue to apply for the purposes of committee business.
Perhaps to save time, I will put the second motion now as well:
That, notwithstanding the Order made February 13, 1986 in relation to the Provisional Standing Orders, those Standing Orders relating to Private Members' Business which were in effect on September 9, 1985 shall remain in force, during the present Session, until the day following the adoption of the report of the Striking Committee establishing the membership of the Standing Committee on Private Members' Business, at which time all items of Private Members' Business on that day's Order Paper shall be placed in a draw to establish an order of precedence for twenty separate items, and they shall be restored to the Order Paper at the stage which they had attained when they appeared on the Order Paper on the day preceding the draw and items not successful in the draw shall be placed on the Order Paper after the order of precedence at the stage they had attained and in the order they had appeared prior to the draw. Provided that all names of Members listed on the Order Paper without notice of items of business shall be dropped from the Order Paper.
